        "original_id": "657bdfd3-be61-5f2b-9ca9-804b7ff44400",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Muehlenbeckia, Euptelea\n- Animal species: Peristoreus viridipennis\n- Plant families: Eupteleaceae\n- Places: Southern Hemisphere, South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, New Zealand, temperate locales north of the equator\n\nFacts:\n- Muehlenbeckia, also called the maidenhair genus, is native to the Southern Hemisphere, especially South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, and New Zealand.\n- Muehlenbeckia has been introduced to temperate locales north of the equator by birds and by cultivation.\n- Euptelea is a genus of two species of flowering plants in the monogeneric family Eupteleaceae.\n- Peristoreus viridipennis is associated with plants of the genus Muehlenbeckia.",
